<code>assert Objects.nonNull(coll) => this.containsAll(coll) && coll.containsAll(this) && this.size() == coll.size();</code>
--------------------
<code>assert Objects.nonNull(coll) => this.equals(new CircularFifoQueue<>(coll));</code>

However, since we need to compare the contents of the queue with the collection without directly using `equals`, we can use the `containsAll` method and check the sizes:

<code>assert Objects.nonNull(coll) => this.size() == coll.size() && this.containsAll(coll);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert coll != null => this.containsAll(coll) && coll.containsAll(this) && this.size() == coll.size();</code>
--------------------
